  "final_message": "The gallery is built: a Flask API under `/api` and a React/Tailwind frontend that the same server serves. I couldn't build the Docker image because `docker` isn't available here.\n\nWhat I did check:\n- **API:** I exercised the endpoints with Flask's test client. That covered register, login, upload, listing, fetching the file bytes back, and delete (including the 401 and 403 cases).\n- **Server:** I ran the app under gunicorn and confirmed `/api/health` and the served frontend.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run build` passes, with `tsc` run first. I didn't click through the UI in a browser.\n\nDetails worth knowing:\n- **Upload rules:** PNG and JPEG are recognised from the file's leading bytes, not the filename. Anything else gets 415 and an error message. Uploads are limited to 10 MB.\n- **Data:** SQLite and the image files live under `data/`; that directory also holds the key that signs login tokens, so tokens survive a restart.\n- **Tokens:** They expire after 30 days.\n- **Errors:** The API returns them as `{\"error\": \"...\"}`; the frontend shows these messages.\n- **Usernames:** Usernames are case-insensitive, 3\u201332 characters, using letters, digits, `_`, `.` or `-`. Passwords must be at least 6 characters.\n- **Build script:** `npm run build` now type-checks before building.\n- **Dependencies:** I added Tailwind and TypeScript to `frontend/package.json` and `package-lock.json`. I didn't add any Python dependencies.\n- **`.gitignore`:** I added one, which the repo didn't have.\n\nThe backend is in `backend/app.py`; the frontend components are in `frontend/src/`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
